# What EAS Build uploads.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore to decide what goes
# into the build archive, so it has to repeat the ordinary ignores as well as
# the extra exclusions below.
#
# This exists because build 12's first attempt failed outright: the archive
# reached 1.3 GB and EAS rejected the upload with a 400. Only mobile/ is needed
# to build the app, but the archive was carrying the Laravel API, both Next.js
# apps, the Go service, and above all the stray nested reelsoo/ checkout - a
# second complete copy of this repository, its own node_modules included.
#
# mobile/ is self-contained (its own package.json and lockfile, no root
# workspace), so excluding every sibling is safe.

# ── The other projects in this monorepo. None builds the iOS app. ───────────
server/
frontend/
admin/
backend-go/
chat-server/

# ── The stray nested duplicate checkout. Not a submodule (there is no
#    .gitmodules), just a second copy of the repo that was never removed - and
#    the single biggest contributor to that 1.3 GB.
reelsoo/

# ── Local-only artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
crashlogs/
*.ips
*.log

# ── Dependencies and build output. The builder installs from the lockfile, so
#    shipping node_modules only makes the upload slower.
**/node_modules/
**/vendor/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.expo/

# The repository's own history: 123 MB, and nothing the builder reads. Written
# as a rooted path on purpose - a leading "**/" only matches .git directories
# NESTED under some parent, so it silently skipped the one at the root, which
# is the only one that mattered.
.git/

# Android build output. The sources stay (an Android build still needs them);
# these are regenerated artefacts that only inflate the upload.
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/app/build/

# ── Secrets. EAS injects real values from its own environment, so a local
#    file must never travel in the archive. The example stays: it documents
#    the variable names and holds no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
